turboexl3_glm53f builds against the mlx-serve plugin kit and turboexl3 (build.zig.zon, by URL and hash). It vendors
no third-party file unchanged. The code below came from other projects and is now this plugin's own code.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlx-serve
https://github.com/ddalcu/mlx-serve
Copyright (c) 2026 David Dalcu
Licensed under the MIT License.

src/streamed/ and src/exl3/ are mlx-serve's GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 bank and its scheduler (from mlx-serve's
src/sdk/weights/streamed/ and src/sdk/quant/exl3/stream/: the bank source, the GLM bank, MiMo's stream bridge, the
routed experts' scheduler, the stream's own SDK and the EXL3 stream quant). They moved out of mlx-serve at bc6c5f2c,
and mlx-serve no longer carries them, so this plugin maintains them. Their imports point at this plugin's files and
the kit. This plugin removed the functions, declarations and tests that it never reaches, and the DeepSeek-V4.1
kernel texts and test fixtures. The stream itself and its read pool are the kit's (`kit.streamed`), not copies.

src/host_shims.zig replaces mlx-serve's sdk/weights/streamed/csrc/mlx_event_shim.cpp, mlx_alloc_shim.cpp,
mlx_launch_cache.inc, mimo_gpu_address.inc and q3_event_shim.mm: it gives their C symbols over the server's host
table. src/csrc/glm53f_gpu_warm.m replaces sdk/weights/streamed/csrc/mimo_gpu_warm.inc: it gives its C symbols and
its kernel's text over Metal's own API. Both are this plugin's code.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlx-stream
https://github.com/davidtai/mlx-stream
Copyright (c) 2026 David Tai
Licensed under the MIT License.

mlx-serve absorbed mlx-stream into its server. The SSD expert streamer, its SDK and the EXL3 stream quant above came
from it. The packed expert record and manifest formats, the streamed-bank layout and the routed-expert EXL3 Metal
kernels are David Tai's earlier work. mlx-serve's NOTICE carries mlx-stream's full entry, with what mlx-stream itself
incorporates (MLX, ExLlamaV3, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/fixtures/config.json is the config.json of a GLM-5.3-Flash sc_3.10bpw streaming repack (turboderp's sc_3.10bpw
branch of https://huggingface.co/turboderp/GLM-5.3-Flash-exl3, with the converter's `expert_streaming` block),
unchanged. [OPEN: the model's licence, from the model card.]

src/glm_tiles.json holds routed-expert tiles of turboderp's GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 packs, used by the tile gate
(src/frac_test.zig). [OPEN: the same licence.]
